     1	# Generalization campaign: three-dataset selection-function measurement
     2	
     3	Branch `generalization/campaign-1` · frozen baseline tag `frozen-2026-08-01` ·
     4	deadline AAS 249 regular abstract Tue 2026-09-30.
     5	
     6	## Claim under test
     7	
     8	The 2026-08-01 ZTF white-dwarf run showed the variance census and the blind
     9	Lomb-Scargle search have complementary selection functions — but on 19
    10	truth-labeled stars, with a known mechanism, and injections conditioned on two
    11	light curves. Red-team verdict: NO-GO as a discovery claim. The flip condition:
    12	run the *frozen* pipeline on independently labeled samples large enough to
    13	measure class-specific completeness and false-positive rate with uncertainty.
    14	This campaign does exactly that and nothing else.
    15	
    16	## Frozen-core / adapter-shell architecture
    17	
    18	- Tag `frozen-2026-08-01` = branch point. Zero edits to any script that
    19	  produced the published bundle; the referee check is an empty
    20	  `git diff frozen-2026-08-01 -- scripts/<frozen five>`.
    21	- Frozen five: `run_catalog_lomb_scargle.py`, `run_lomb_scargle.py`,
    22	  `lomb_scargle_common.py`, `build_catalog_panels.py`,
    23	  `fetch_catalog_lightcurves.py`. SHA-256 pinned in
    24	  `scripts/generalization/frozen_api.py`; `assert_frozen()` runs at import and
    25	  at the top of every campaign script.
    26	- Campaign code lives in `scripts/generalization/` and imports the frozen
    27	  callables only through `frozen_api`. The frozen CLI never runs on campaign
    28	  data (its `main()` merges the WD roster and rewrites the published table);
    29	  `verify_cli_identity.py` proves the import path is byte-identical to the
    30	  CLI's internal call path.
    31	- Known frozen quirks are pinned by `tests/test_frozen_constants.py`, fixed by
    32	  nothing: the `>= 2.5` vs `> 2.5` census inconsistency (provably
    33	  non-affecting: 0 of 5,568 published ratios within 1e-4 of 2.5; campaign
    34	  metrics use `>=` and assert no campaign ratio equals 2.5 exactly), the
    35	  bootstrap's `int(source_id[-9:])` seed (harmless for 19-digit numeric
    36	  campaign ids by construction), duplicated pass-bound literals (AST-scan
    37	  test).
    38	
    39	### Campaign source_id convention
    40	
    41	19-digit numeric strings: `90…` D3 targets, `92…` D2 arm B, `93…` D2 arm A,
    42	`94…` D2 statistical nulls. No collision with Gaia DR3 ids; always valid for
    43	the frozen seed convention.
    44	
    45	### Replay gate (blocks everything)
    46	
    47	`replay_gate.py` re-runs the frozen `analyze_star` through `frozen_api` on 25
    48	published stars (all 7 schema-v2 + 18 stride-sampled schema-v1) and
    49	byte-compares against the committed bundle. Comparison tiers: raw-identical;
    50	identical after CRLF→LF normalization (git stored the bundle normalized);
    51	identical after the documented v1→v2 schema transform — 921/928 published
    52	files were written before commit `fa16d7f`, which added the
    53	`available`/`unavailable_reason` keys and bumped `schema_version` 1→2 while
    54	changing no numeric code path (diff on record). Gate passes only with zero
    55	mismatches AND at least one schema-v2 star reproducing with no transform.
    56	Campaign L-S runs are valid only on machine+env pairs that passed the gate.
    57	
    58	### Environment
    59	
    60	The published run's venv (laptop `jacks-7i-5090`) is recorded in
    61	`generalization/env/FROZEN_ENV.md`; the numerics-bearing subset is pinned in
    62	`requirements-frozen.txt` (Python 3.12.12, numpy 2.3.x, scipy 1.16.3, astropy
    63	8.0.1, iers-data 0.2026.7.27, pyerfa 2.0.1.5, pandas 2.3.3). Discrepancy on
    64	record: pip metadata said numpy 2.3.3 but the venv imports 2.3.5; the replay
    65	gate verdict on that venv is the authority on whether the published numbers
    66	reproduce under what is actually installed. requirements-frozen.txt is updated
    67	to whatever passes the gate, and the manifest of every campaign run records
    68	`env_versions()` at runtime.
    69	
    70	## D1 — ZTF white dwarfs (anchor, done)
    71	
    72	The published 2026-08-01 bundle: 19-star truth roster + 928-star catalog.
    73	No re-run; campaign metrics re-read the published per-star JSONs.
    74	
    75	## D3 — ZTF × Kepler delta Scuti (real ZTF light curves, external labels)
    76	
    77	- Labels: Murphy+2019 (VizieR J/MNRAS/485/2380/table1, 14,330 Kepler A/F
    78	  stars; `dSct` flag 0/1/2 — ships its own labeled negative class).
    79	- Amplitude axis: Mo+2026 (J/A+A/710/A245): table2 = 259,883 extracted
    80	  frequencies (SNR>8) for 1,838 delta Scutis → per-star dominant amplitude
    81	  (ppt × 1.0857 → mmag); table1 = confirmed super-Nyquist modes → the
    82	  sub-hour stratum (any confirmed SNF ⇒ real mode above Kepler LC Nyquist
    83	  283.2 µHz ⇒ P < 59 min). This replaces the originally scouted Bowman+2016
    84	  join: Bowman's VizieR table carries no amplitudes; Mo+2026 supersedes it
    85	  (and is itself the published Murphy×Bowman merge, 1,838 stars).
    86	- Roster (`build_d3_roster.py`, built 2026-08-28, deterministic, no RNG):
    87	  gmag ≥ 13.2 (ZTF saturation), ALL 610 dSct=1 survivors + ALL 76 dSct=2
    88	  (own class, excluded from headline numbers) + 2,314 dSct=0 negatives
    89	  stride-sampled in KIC order = 3,000. Amplitude coverage of positives:
    90	  456/610 with dominant amplitude; 48 > 10 mmag; 254 in 1–10; 154 < 1;
    91	  290 sub-hour; median 1.77 mmag. The 1–10 mmag log ladder and the
    92	  sub-threshold majority make the completeness turn-on curve the headline
    93	  D3 deliverable, not a defect (pre-registered: risk 2).
    94	- Acquisition: frozen `fetch_catalog_lightcurves.py --roster roster_d3.csv`
    95	  verbatim (10″ cone, 1.25 s cadence, resumable); frozen QC chain via
    96	  `build_panels_generic.py` (nearest-cluster crossmatch, catflags/chi cuts,
    97	  ≥20 exp/band, BJD_TDB at Palomar — all frozen functions).
    98	- Prespecified subsets: crowding (sep < 1.0″, ≤3 objects in cone),
    99	  near-saturation (g < 14 flagged; g > 14 safe subset).
   100	- Caveat on record: dSct=0 means "not a delta Scuti", not "constant" —
   101	  D3 FPR is an upper bound.
   102	
   103	## D2 — TESS-truth transplant (DAV signals in real ZTF windows)
   104	
   105	- Truth: Romero+2022 (MNRAS 511, 1574; arXiv:2201.04158; 74 new DAVs,
   106	  TESS Cy1–3) + Romero+2025 (ApJ 984, 112; arXiv:2407.07260; 32 new DAVs,
   107	  Cy4–5). Published per-mode tables: period [s] + amplitude [ppt] + per-star
   108	  FAP(1/1000) limit + 20-s-cadence flags. 2025 revisions apply: NOV
   109	  retractions (TIC 261400271, 804835539, 317620456) and updated mode lists
   110	  for re-observed 2022 objects — latest published solution wins.
   111	- Truth model, not interpolation (`d2_truth_model.py`): DAV P < 240 s is
   112	  super-Nyquist AND past the first sinc null of TESS 120-s data; the mode
   113	  table is evaluated analytically at the template's real `bjd_tdb`.
   114	  Chain: ppt → mag (×1.0857e-3) → de-dilution OFF by default (SPOC PDCSAP is
   115	  crowding-corrected; ON = prespecified variant) → de-integrate TESS sinc
   116	  (reject modes with |sinc| < 0.3, i.e. P < 197 s from 120-s data; prefer
   117	  20-s cadence solutions) → bandpass ladder A_g/A_TESS ∈ {1.4, 1.7, 2.1} ×
   118	  A_r/A_g ∈ {0.70, 0.80, 0.90} (nominal 1.7/0.80 from an in-code blackbody
   119	  derivative; the ladder is non-optional — zr carries most published
   120	  confirmations) → re-integrate ZTF 30-s sinc analytically → compose
   121	  phase-coherently in zg and zr (shared t_ref) so the frozen two-band rule
   122	  keeps its meaning.
   123	- Windows: templates from the 510 not-detected stars of the published run,
   124	  matched by median zg mag (|Δg| ≤ 0.25), K=3 templates per target at
   125	  10/50/90th percentile of exposures-per-night (75% of zg nights are
   126	  single-exposure; per-night median subtraction annihilates 53% of zg data —
   127	  D2 largely measures that penalty; pre-registered, stratified: risk 3).
   128	- Arms: B primary (signal + real ZTF mags, real magerr), A diagnostic
   129	  (synthetic Gaussian floor). FPR: 1,000 arm-A zero-amplitude nulls over
   130	  1,000 distinct real windows (Wilson upper ~0.4% at zero confirmed);
   131	  arm-B nulls are tautological (templates ARE the not-detected set).
   132	  Verification arm: ~20 SPOC light curves prewhitened to confirm published
   133	  solutions; everything else needs metadata only.
   134	
   135	## Metrics — see METRICS_SPEC.md (frozen before any campaign L-S run)
   136	
   137	## Execution topology
   138	
   139	- Mac: rosters, fetches, shard building, metrics, figures, git (authoritative).
