     1	# METRICS_SPEC — frozen before any campaign Lomb-Scargle run
     2	
     3	Implemented by `scripts/generalization/metrics_generalization.py`. Any change
     4	to this file after the first campaign L-S run voids the prespecification and
     5	must be reported as such.
     6	
     7	## Inputs
     8	
     9	Per-star JSONs from `run_generalization_ls.py` (never only a summary CSV:
    10	`overall_result` collapses the two passes and can report a spuriously low
    11	best pass). For each star and each pass (`low`, `high`) the JSON carries the
    12	best candidate, the 15 stored `top_peaks` (5 zg + 5 zr + 5 multiband), FAPs,
    13	amplitudes, A95 limits, alias flags, and availability. Census rows come from
    14	`build_panels_generic.py` output (D3) or the frozen published census (D1).
    15	
    16	## Frequency-match definitions
    17	
    18	- Tolerance: `1.5 / baseline_days` per star — the pipeline's own alias/window
    19	  tolerance, adopted verbatim. `baseline_days` from the star JSON.
    20	- `matched_primary`: the pipeline's best candidate frequency within tolerance
    21	  of any truth frequency (D3: Mo+2026 frequencies for that KIC, else the
    22	  dominant; D2: the injected mode list).
    23	- `matched_any_mode`: ANY of the 15 stored top_peaks within tolerance of any
    24	  truth frequency.
    25	- Harmonics: matches at 2f and f/2 are logged separately
    26	  (`matched_harmonic`), never counted in the headline.
    27	- Truth frequencies for D3 stars without Mo+2026 rows: no frequency scoring;
    28	  the star contributes to detection-level completeness only
    29	  (`freq_scorable = False` in the per-star table).
    30	
    31	## Detection rules (all four always reported)
    32	
    33	1. `confirmed` — headline: blind status == confirmed.
    34	2. `confirmed|candidate` — permissive: status in {confirmed, candidate}.
    35	3. `census` — frozen census flag (any of six ratios >= 2.5).
    36	4. `either` — (1) OR (3): the complementarity number.
    37	
    38	## Headline estimands
    39	
    40	- **Completeness** (per class × pass × rule):
    41	  P(detected AND matched_primary | labeled positive) for rules 1–2;
    42	  P(census flag | labeled positive) for rule 3; rule 4 uses rule 1's
    43	  frequency requirement on the L-S side.
    44	  Also reported without the frequency requirement (detection-only), to
    45	  decompose "missed" vs "found at wrong frequency".
    46	- **Purity**: P(matched_primary | detected) among labeled positives, and
    47	  among all stars with truth frequencies.
    48	- **FPR** (per rule): P(detected | labeled negative). D3: dSct=0 class
    49	  (upper bound; stated). D2: 1,000 arm-A zero-amplitude nulls (statistical).
    50	  FP frequency distribution plotted for the alias-veto audit; alias-blanking
    51	  rate reported as a diagnostic (expected 0.03–0.15% per star).
    52	- **Intervals**: Wilson 95% on every proportion, inline in every table.
    53	- **Contingency + McNemar** (census vs L-S on positives) per dataset — the
    54	  complementarity claim in quantified form.
    55	- **Completeness surfaces**: (log P, log A_g) and (exposures-per-night,
    56	  log A_g) bins; per-cell Wilson intervals; D3 also vs the amplitude ladder
    57	  strata from the roster.
    58	- **Sensitivity**: every D2 ladder variant (3×3 bandpass × de-dilution
    59	  on/off) and every prespecified D3 subset (crowding, near-saturation,
    60	  safe) reported alongside the nominal; headline quoted as the band across
    61	  the ladder, not a single number.
    62	
    63	## Guards
    64	
    65	- Assert no campaign census ratio equals 2.5 exactly (the frozen `>=`/`>`
    66	  inconsistency is non-affecting on D1; this keeps it provably so on campaign
    67	  data).
    68	- Assert every input JSON has `complete == true` and both passes; stars with
    69	  unavailable passes are tabulated separately, never dropped silently.
    70	- Manifest: SHA-256 of every input file, env versions, frozen-file SHAs,
    71	  spec version (git blob SHA of this file at run time).
    72	
    73	## Outputs
    74	
    75	`generalization/results/<date>_<dataset>/metrics/`:
    76	per_star.csv, completeness_by_class_pass_rule.csv, contingency_mcnemar.json,
    77	fpr.csv, fp_frequency_distribution.csv, surfaces/*.csv, sensitivity.csv,
    78	manifest.json. Figures via `plot_generalization.py` from these CSVs only.

